1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:47,714
You reek of alcohol.

3
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,883
I'm sorry.

4
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:16,701
Get off me.

5
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:26,461
I swear, it was so dark in here
I couldn't see a thing.

6
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:28,338
Besides, I'm really drunk right now.

7
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:29,506
Enough. Just get out.

8
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:30,632
Okay.

9
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:35,553
-Don't you need a hand getting up--
-I said get out!

10
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:44,104
Well, that sobered me up.

11
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:49,984
Damn it.

12
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:55,698
Huh?

13
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:18,930
Why is this…

14
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:25,562
Mr. Baek.

15
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:29,357
Sir.

16
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:33,027
Sir…

17
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:38,158
Sir.

18
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:42,078
Ms. Na.

19
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:43,621
Why is she here?

20
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:47,208
Ms. Na.

21
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,045
She reeks of alcohol.

22
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:00,805
Ms. Na.

23
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,226
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

24
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,561
-What are you doing?
-Ms…

25
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:10,190
Sir.

26
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,194
What's wrong?

27
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:18,573
Are you hurt?

28
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:23,119
The power went out yesterday,
and I fell in the bathroom.

29
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:28,499
That's why the digital locks on the gate
and front door weren't working.

30
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,834
Huh?

31
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:33,630
-The digital locks are broken?
-Yes.

32
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:41,429
Why is that woman lying there?

33
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:42,889
You didn't know?

34
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:46,684
I'll wake her up now.

35
00:03:47,852 --> 00:03:48,770
Don't bother.

36
00:03:50,688 --> 00:03:51,522
Leave her alone.

37
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:16,464
A power outage and broken locks.

38
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,343
This doesn't seem like a coincidence.

39
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:23,096
This has to be Choi Do-yoon's doing.

40
00:04:23,888 --> 00:04:25,098
Call a repairman first.

41
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:26,766
Yes, sir.

42
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,686
May I ask why Ms. Na is…

43
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:31,145
Huh? What?

44
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:34,023
What about her?
Nothing happened between us yesterday.

45
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:36,109
-Pardon?
-What?

46
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:38,069
Nothing, sir.

47
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:39,654
Never mind.

48
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:43,366
Shouldn't you see a doctor first?

49
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:46,953
I just twisted it a little.

50
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:49,330
It's much better than it was yesterday.

51
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:50,248
I see.

52
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:53,835
I'll get the locks fixed
before your family arrives.

53
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:57,380
-They're coming?
-Did you forget?

54
00:04:57,463 --> 00:05:00,091
Your family's coming
to celebrate your birthday.

55
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:05,263
Right.

56
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:09,017
I'm worried you hit your head
when you fell yesterday.

57
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,184
What are you doing?

58
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:11,185
Your head--

59
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:16,065
I'll be inside.
Come in when you're done here.

60
00:05:36,627 --> 00:05:38,713
I'm sorry.

61
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:48,389
Hello.

62
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:54,645
You slept on the couch last night.
I guess you were pretty drunk.

63
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:58,858
Yeah, I was so drunk
I don't remember anything.

64
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:01,110
I woke up wondering
why I was sleeping there.

65
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:15,541
Gosh.

66
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,835
Your chest is limping. Are you okay?

67
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,045
Yeah, I'm…

68
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:23,257
-"Chest"?
-What?

69
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:26,177
You just said my chest is limping.

70
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:28,513
Your ankle.

71
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:31,974
I asked if your ankle was okay. Ankle.

72
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:37,980
Yeah, it's just a bit swollen.

73
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,148
That's a relief.

74
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:40,483
Yeah.

75
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:43,653
I guess I'll have some breakfast.

76
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:52,245
You should eat out.
My family will be here soon.

77
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:54,122
Your family? Why?

78
00:06:54,872 --> 00:06:56,332
It's my birthday today.

79
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,085
Your birthday?

80
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:00,878
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

81
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:03,256
Well, why should I tell you?

82
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:05,049
That's no way to spend a birthday.

83
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:08,344
If I'd known it was your birthday,
I could've gotten you a little something.

84
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:11,681
I don't need a gift from you.

85
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:14,559
Did you really have to put it like that?

86
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:18,438
Fine. If you don't need one,
I won't bother.

87
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:20,648
Wait.

88
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,077
Your chest…

89
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:38,207
I'm sorry.

90
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:41,794
I was just going to tell you
to take off the rubber glove.

91
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,754
You were just so light.

92
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:47,633
It's just that I have no core strength.
Yeah, I should take this off.

93
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:49,051
Wow.

94
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:51,929
What am I looking at?

95
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,556
How did you even get…

96
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:57,393
Gotta lock those doors, Ho-rang.

97
00:07:57,477 --> 00:08:00,771
Or bad guys like me
will just walk right in.

98
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:04,525
Girlfriend?

99
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:05,985
Doesn't look like it.

100
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:07,403
A one-night stand?

101
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:09,405
Probably a bit low-rent.

102
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,657
-Hey, Choi Do-yoon.
-I'm his secretary.

103
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,160
-Secretary?
-Yes.

104
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:15,745
Mr. Baek…

105
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:18,247
Our senior managing director
got hurt yesterday,

106
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:20,208
so I came by on my day off.

107
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,585
He got hurt? How?

108
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:25,004
There was a power outage here yesterday.

109
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:27,215
He could've been seriously hurt.

110
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:29,300
Well, I'll be on my way.

111
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:31,719
Happy birthday, sir.

112
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:51,739
Wait.

113
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,242
I should've brought my laptop.

114
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,827
Oh, shoot.

115
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:29,318
I guess you weren't hurt that badly.

116
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:33,197
I'm sure you've been hoping I'd die.

117
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:34,865
Sorry for being perfectly fine.

118
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:37,159
How can you say something so horrible?

119
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:40,705
Horrible? I thought you, of all people,
would be unfazed.

120
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:42,832
What does that mean?

121
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,668
You can't possibly have forgotten.

122
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,336
Or can you?

123
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,065
Hello.

124
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,817
Why are you limping?

125
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,152
I just twisted my ankle.

126
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:13,529
Did you know your lock's broken?

127
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:17,325
Don't you know people like us
have to keep security tight?

128
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:20,578
I'm getting it fixed today.
Thanks for your concern, Aunt.

129
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:23,831
It shows a lack of competence.

130
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:45,978
Damn it.

131
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:09,085
Oh no. Are you okay, Ms. Secretary?

132
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,546
I wonder why you're eating ramyeon

133
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:16,008
at the convenience store outside
Ho-rang's house instead of going home.

134
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,635
I'm really curious.

135
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:20,012
I was starving after working so hard.

136
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:21,639
Cut the nonsense.

137
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:25,893
You're not really his secretary.
You two have something going on, right?

138
00:11:25,976 --> 00:11:26,811
Sorry?

139
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:29,605
To celebrate his birthday, did you two…

140
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:31,482
hook up?

141
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:35,653
What's wrong?
Did I hit a little too close to home?

142
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:39,824
Baek Ho-rang has unexpected taste.
Going for something like this.

143
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:41,826
"Something like this"?

144
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:43,953
So you've got some pride in you, huh?

145
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:45,579
I guess that's kind of cute.

146
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:47,873
How about

147
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:51,001
you go out with me?

148
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,587
I can do better than that clueless idiot.

149
00:11:57,007 --> 00:11:59,802
-Excuse me, Mr. Baek Ho-rang's cousin.
-Yeah?

150
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:03,180
Just call me Choi Do-yoon.

151
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:06,517
Look at you giving your name
without a shred of shame.

152
00:12:16,736 --> 00:12:18,571
I've lost my appetite. I'm done eating.

153
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:21,198
Smells like burning trash in here.

154
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:23,159
Damn it.

155
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:25,911
What the hell?

156
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:27,913
What was that? Seriously.

157
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:34,545
Are you really turning this down?
You'd be the face of TS.

158
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:37,840
This is a huge opportunity, Eun-ho.

159
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:40,509
Hanlim is involved in this TS project too.

160
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:42,178
We're planning your US debut.

161
00:12:42,261 --> 00:12:45,514
Becoming the face of TS Resort
would be a huge boost.

162
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:48,434
How long are you going to stick
to PSAs and charity ads?

163
00:12:48,517 --> 00:12:50,895
I want to make a positive impact
as an actor.

164
00:12:51,729 --> 00:12:55,441
What's the point of being successful
if I can't choose my projects?

165
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:58,944
It was never about fame or money.
You know that.

166
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:03,324
That's our point. To do more projects,
you need this kind of exposure.

167
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:04,992
It's a positive cycle.

168
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:06,786
More success, more impact.

169
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,121
He's right, Eun-ho. Let's do the ad.

170
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:13,459
You're only promoting your movie
and reviewing scripts, so you have time.

171
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:22,176
Let me decide after I see the concept.

172
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:29,558
Why did you bring so much food?

173
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:32,353
Eating well and taking care of yourself
is a skill too.

174
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:33,687
Just eat.

175
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,857
I eat well. I have a housekeeper.

176
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:39,318
This galbijjim came from Dojaewon
early this morning.

177
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,071
This one came from our hotel
early this morning too.

178
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:44,073
Nothing like your housekeeper's cooking.

179
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:45,908
Have some tact.

180
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:47,910
Thanks for looking out for me, Aunt.

181
00:13:50,329 --> 00:13:53,040
Just look at that smug grin. You brat.

182
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:56,043
Mom, he's doing it on purpose.

183
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:59,213
You don't have to bring food
from TS Hotel.

184
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:02,424
I hear it's been tough there lately.

185
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:09,098
What's wrong with our hotel?
Isn't TS Resort the one struggling?

186
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,559
No, I heard the hotel's F&amp;B side is…

187
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:16,397
already swamped.

188
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:19,942
I feel bad increasing their workload
for my birthday.

189
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,485
Anything going on at the hotel?

190
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:22,403
Huh?

191
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:26,073
Of course not. Why would there be?

192
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:28,158
It's the same as always.

193
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:32,204
Isn't the hotel busy preparing
for the 30th anniversary?

194
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:33,747
Oh, that?

195
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:35,291
Right, of course.

196
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:38,085
Yeah, we're busy, but…

197
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:39,837
What is wrong with you?

198
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,088
Let me get that.

199
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:42,965
Hey, get me a spoon!

200
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:48,470
Do-yoon, why is your hand so red?
Oh my, you're shaking too.

201
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:51,223
I guess I have a bit of a tremor
from exhaustion lately.

202
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:54,059
-It's nothing.
-You're shaking like you got electrocuted.

203
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:55,394
I'm fine.

204
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:56,562
Go ahead and eat.

205
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:58,272
Ho-rang.

206
00:14:58,355 --> 00:14:59,481
Yes, Grandma.

207
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:02,693
-I invited a guest over.
-A guest?

208
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:25,132
I think we got them, ma'am.

209
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,010
That looks good.
Thank you. I'm counting on you.

210
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:30,971
I'll pick the photos and get back to you.

211
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:36,310
Wow. Is she a celebrity?

212
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,189
Or a chaebol?

213
00:15:41,106 --> 00:15:42,524
She's so pretty.

214
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:54,495
There's been talk
of you two getting married.

215
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:57,831
I thought it'd be nice if she joined us,
so I invited her.

216
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,250
Happy birthday, Mr. Baek.

217
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:02,336
-Oh.
-Here's your present.

218
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:03,754
Thank you.

219
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:05,673
Seol-hee, you get prettier every day.

220
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:08,258
You look like a model,
not someone from an ad agency.

221
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:09,301
Very gorgeous.

222
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:12,763
Hanlim Advertising Company
seems pretty solid lately.

223
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:16,392
Everyone around me lights up
when Hanlim's stock is mentioned.

224
00:16:17,893 --> 00:16:20,771
You two are close, right?
You should sit facing each other.

225
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,606
-Good idea.
-Let him sit there.

226
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:23,774
It's fine.

227
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:29,071
Let's eat.

228
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,616
Thank you for the meal.

229
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:55,848
If I had my laptop with me,
I could've gotten some writing done.

230
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:03,480
Maybe I'll just read a web novel.

231
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:05,983
Huh?

232
00:17:06,483 --> 00:17:08,861
Hey, this is the chaebol
you're charging, right?

233
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:09,778
Huh?

234
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:11,905
"Baek Ho-rang"?

235
00:17:12,948 --> 00:17:15,409
BAEK HO-RANG AND HAN SEOL-HEE
ANNOUNCE ENGAGEMENT

236
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:27,838
Did you have to do this today of all days?

237
00:17:27,921 --> 00:17:30,883
Talks of your marriage
have been ongoing for years.

238
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:33,594
Even so, you announced it
without consulting me.

239
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:35,054
That's what I'm saying.

240
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,764
This isn't right, Mom!

241
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:39,391
A third-gen chaebol marriage announcement

242
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:43,353
is basically a PR move
to announce Ho-rang will inherit TS!

243
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:45,230
You know that, Mom!

244
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:50,694
Mother, in this day and age,

245
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:53,614
you can't force Ho-rang
into a marriage he doesn't want.

246
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:55,908
I mean, Ho-rang's already quite sensitive.

247
00:17:55,991 --> 00:17:58,452
Look at him. He hurt his ankle.

248
00:17:58,535 --> 00:18:00,954
All because he didn't have
someone there for him.

249
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:03,207
It's a good thing it was just his ankle.

250
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:05,000
It could've been worse.

251
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:08,337
-It was just a coincidence--
-So was your mom and dad's accident.

252
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:18,764
You never know
when or how someone might go down.

253
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:22,226
The more people you have around
to cover your weaknesses,

254
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:24,770
the more chess pieces you have
to back you up,

255
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:27,231
the better off you'll be.

256
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:32,152
I know what's good for me.
I'll decide for myself.

257
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,404
-Stop being so stubborn.
-No.

258
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:36,323
You should stop being stubborn, Grandma.

259
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:39,868
I'll issue a correction.

260
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,329
You should go home now.

261
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,168
Take down all the articles

262
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:52,422
and issue a correction saying
I will never marry Director Han.

263
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:55,676
Sir.

264
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:58,137
I think you should see this.

265
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:02,224
The engagement article
is getting positive reactions.

266
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:05,144
The stock price, which had been falling,
is now rebounding.

267
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:08,063
Should we issue a correction?

268
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:12,526
Think like Senior Managing Director Baek,
not Baek Ho-rang.

269
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:14,069
What would you do?

270
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:16,989
Grandma.

271
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:20,576
Seol-hee aside,
if you marry into the Hanlim family,

272
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:23,412
it'll be much easier
for TS Resort and TS Hotel

273
00:19:23,495 --> 00:19:26,623
to enter overseas markets.

274
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,667
I'm already working on expanding overseas.

275
00:19:29,376 --> 00:19:30,377
Please.

276
00:19:32,212 --> 00:19:34,673
Can't you respect my wishes
just this once?

277
00:19:34,756 --> 00:19:37,885
If you can think and act
more strategically than I can,

278
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:39,219
then by all means.

279
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:43,056
Were you like this with my parents too?
Right up to the accident?

280
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,437
I didn't have to push them.

281
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,314
They did it all on their own.

282
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,819
Marry Seol-hee.

283
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:10,417
Sir, about the articles…

284
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:11,877
Leave them.

285
00:20:12,669 --> 00:20:13,545
Then…

286
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:17,174
I'll just have to do
Hanlim's part too, right?

287
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:28,227
This is exhausting, Mom.

288
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:30,229
Ho-rang's not a kid anymore.

289
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:33,774
How long will you keep serving him
lavish meals like a VIP?

290
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:36,318
She's right, Mother.
It's a lot of work for you.

291
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:38,987
Next time,
let's just eat out or get him a gift--

292
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:41,531
If you don't want to come,
don't bother coming.

293
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:44,534
Mom, I was just worried about you.

294
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:46,286
Come on, you're hurting my feelings.

295
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:08,767
Mr. Kim!

296
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:10,727
You were here?

297
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:29,538
PORTABLE CHARGER

298
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:38,380
The person you're calling is unavailable.

299
00:22:12,956 --> 00:22:16,168
How long is she going to stay out? Jeez.

300
00:22:37,606 --> 00:22:38,482
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

301
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:46,615
What are you doing?

302
00:22:46,698 --> 00:22:48,658
Why weren't you answering? Where were you?

303
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:51,995
I guess I didn't notice.
It was in my back pocket.

304
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:55,582
Why are you so mad?
Were you waiting for me?

305
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:56,750
Waiting for you? As if.

306
00:22:58,126 --> 00:23:00,087
It was late, and I couldn't reach you, so…

307
00:23:00,837 --> 00:23:02,005
The battery!

308
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:05,258
I need to charge my heart battery.

309
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:10,472
I walked around the neighborhood for hours
because of you.

310
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:14,101
My family left after lunch.

311
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:16,144
They did?

312
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:19,314
My family spends all day together
on birthdays.

313
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:21,566
I should've come earlier, then.

314
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:24,736
Anyway, I need to charge my battery,
so let's go in.

315
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:29,699
Mr. Baek!

316
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:30,742
What is it?

317
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,661
Hey, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

318
00:23:36,123 --> 00:23:37,541
Ta-da!

319
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:44,089
It's your birthday.
We can't just let it pass.

320
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:46,716
I'll sing for you, so make a wish.

321
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:50,846
Here's a special song
selected just for you.

322
00:23:55,308 --> 00:23:58,603
It's Ho-rang the tiger's birthday

323
00:23:59,187 --> 00:24:02,816
The brave hero of the mountains

324
00:24:02,899 --> 00:24:06,069
-All the animals gather in the park
-All the animals gather in the park

325
00:24:06,153 --> 00:24:09,114
And the grand ball begins

326
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:12,659
The rabbit dances

327
00:24:12,742 --> 00:24:15,871
And the fox plays the violin

328
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:19,082
Skippy-skip

329
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:23,086
Skippy-skipping around

330
00:24:25,046 --> 00:24:26,131
Did you make a wish?

331
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:28,842
Go on. Blow out the candle
and make a wish.

332
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:35,974
Happy birthday.

333
00:24:39,352 --> 00:24:40,228
Why…

334
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:44,191
Why that song?

335
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:49,154
Well, it's the first song I think of
when I hear your name.

336
00:24:54,326 --> 00:24:57,579
What's this?
Why do you look so shocked and moved?

337
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:03,126
Did I just become the heroine
who brought back

338
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:06,004
your happy childhood memories?

339
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,594
I think it's raining.

340
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:13,970
Come on. Let's go eat cake.

341
00:25:31,112 --> 00:25:32,822
I read that article.

342
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:36,993
That's…

343
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:39,454
Is it one of those
arranged chaebol marriages?

344
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:43,375
You said you had no one else
and you'd help me with romance.

345
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:46,086
Isn't this a breach of contract?

346
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:47,754
No, it's not.

347
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:50,048
That article was my grandmother's doing,

348
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:53,385
and that marriage isn't happening.

349
00:25:53,468 --> 00:25:55,345
We'll issue a correction in due course.

350
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,556
I see.

351
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:00,183
I mean it.

352
00:26:00,684 --> 00:26:02,227
My grandmother is…

353
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:07,148
She can be a bit overbearing.

354
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:09,859
I'll take care of it.

355
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:12,654
Don't believe anything you hear
about me getting married.

356
00:26:15,615 --> 00:26:18,618
Did your grandmother name you
Baek Ho-rang?

357
00:26:23,498 --> 00:26:24,374
No.

358
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:26,042
My parents did.

359
00:26:27,711 --> 00:26:29,462
Why did they name you Ho-rang?

360
00:26:31,131 --> 00:26:33,800
My father dreamed of a white tiger
before I was born.

361
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:37,178
The white tiger, the baekho,
was in my mother's arms.

362
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:42,142
That suits your surname perfectly.
They gave you a great name.

363
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:46,646
As for my birth dream,

364
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:50,900
it was a tree with all kinds of fruit
hanging from its branches.

365
00:26:50,984 --> 00:26:54,112
My mom said it looked so rare and special

366
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:56,323
that she named me Bo-bae,
meaning "precious."

367
00:26:57,365 --> 00:26:58,533
What a lovely dream.

368
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:01,036
But

369
00:27:02,495 --> 00:27:03,538
why do you ask?

370
00:27:05,540 --> 00:27:07,167
To be honest,

371
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:10,128
I think a birth dream is just a dream
that seems special.

372
00:27:10,211 --> 00:27:13,089
I don't think they symbolize anything.

373
00:27:13,715 --> 00:27:15,967
But that's true love
right there, isn't it?

374
00:27:16,551 --> 00:27:19,095
Giving your child
the very best of everything,

375
00:27:19,179 --> 00:27:21,222
starting with your dream.

376
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:26,436
So, happy birthday.

377
00:27:26,936 --> 00:27:30,315
Mr. Baek Ho-rang, whose parents gave him
the gift of a white tiger dream.

378
00:27:36,112 --> 00:27:37,572
As for your grandma…

379
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:40,617
I don't think she's overbearing
for no reason.

380
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:43,328
She's probably just looking out for you.

381
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:47,082
She went about it the wrong way,

382
00:27:47,582 --> 00:27:49,668
but it comes from a place of love.

383
00:28:00,136 --> 00:28:01,346
When I was a kid,

384
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,265
I lost my parents in an accident.

385
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:08,853
They were on their way to see me
when it happened.

386
00:28:09,854 --> 00:28:13,692
As soon as the press found out,
they barged into my hospital room.

387
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,696
Pushing cameras right in my face.

388
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:22,450
Some paparazzi even dressed up
as doctors or nurses to get in.

389
00:28:23,451 --> 00:28:24,786
So I get a little sensitive.

390
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:27,706
Like yesterday, at the hospital.

391
00:28:28,957 --> 00:28:30,166
Situations like that.

392
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:33,586
I didn't know.

393
00:28:44,013 --> 00:28:44,848
What was that?

394
00:28:45,932 --> 00:28:47,642
You've had it on you for a while.

395
00:28:54,524 --> 00:28:56,568
You should have told me.

396
00:28:56,651 --> 00:28:58,737
It's all in the past.

397
00:29:03,158 --> 00:29:04,409
Don't do it.

398
00:29:05,326 --> 00:29:06,870
Don't do what?

399
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:11,499
You were about to comfort me, weren't you?

400
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:16,087
It doesn't really resonate with me
or comfort me, so don't.

401
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:20,091
You're really cynical, aren't you?

402
00:29:20,884 --> 00:29:23,261
It's not like I was going to be rude.

403
00:29:23,344 --> 00:29:26,598
I was trying to comfort you,
but you still didn't like it.

404
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:32,687
I wasn't going to say
anything that comforting anyway.

405
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:36,274
But you looked at me so tenderly.

406
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:40,153
I wasn't looking at you to comfort you.

407
00:29:40,236 --> 00:29:41,404
Then what?

408
00:30:08,848 --> 00:30:10,892
What's wrong with my heart?

409
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:03,069
Oh, I…

410
00:31:03,152 --> 00:31:05,655
I'm getting tipsy.
I should go to bed. Good night.

411
00:31:18,209 --> 00:31:20,587
Why is my heart beating so fast?

412
00:31:21,129 --> 00:31:23,089
My heart has never beaten this fast

413
00:31:23,172 --> 00:31:25,675
except when I electrocuted someone
and knocked them out.

414
00:31:45,069 --> 00:31:48,114
Honestly, the mood was a little…

415
00:31:50,116 --> 00:31:51,659
something, wasn't it?

416
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:57,123
It felt like we were about to kiss.

417
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:03,630
This is it.

418
00:32:03,713 --> 00:32:05,131
Yes, this is it.

419
00:32:05,214 --> 00:32:06,591
I need to write this down!

420
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:49,425
Is it broken?

421
00:33:08,277 --> 00:33:11,114
Your call can't be connected.
Leave a message after the tone.

422
00:33:11,197 --> 00:33:12,824
SEOL-HEE

423
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:28,631
Hey, it's me.

424
00:33:28,715 --> 00:33:31,259
That woman hanging around Baek Ho-rang.

425
00:33:35,221 --> 00:33:36,556
Is she really his secretary?

426
00:34:15,136 --> 00:34:19,724
These are all just
distracting thoughts and worries.

427
00:35:10,983 --> 00:35:12,151
No.

428
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:43,724
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

429
00:36:03,411 --> 00:36:04,787
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

430
00:36:50,708 --> 00:36:53,252
My gosh. What are you doing?

431
00:36:53,753 --> 00:36:54,670
You scared me.

432
00:36:56,130 --> 00:36:57,215
Well…

433
00:36:58,299 --> 00:37:01,219
It was time to charge,
but you didn't come.

434
00:37:07,725 --> 00:37:09,685
But how did you get in here?

435
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:13,814
Did you pick the lock?

436
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:15,441
What do you take me for?

437
00:37:15,524 --> 00:37:17,610
The door was open!

438
00:37:17,693 --> 00:37:20,571
Even if it was open,
why would you enter a woman's room?

439
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:22,365
A woman's room? Please.

440
00:37:22,448 --> 00:37:23,449
This is my garage.

441
00:37:23,532 --> 00:37:25,826
And you are my portable charger
under contract.

442
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:28,329
Nothing more, nothing less.

443
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:31,749
That woke me right up.

444
00:37:32,416 --> 00:37:33,626
Hey, excuse me?

445
00:37:33,709 --> 00:37:35,878
Who touches
a portable charger's lips like…

446
00:37:39,382 --> 00:37:40,675
Like this?

447
00:37:40,758 --> 00:37:41,717
Who does that?

448
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:46,347
That was…

449
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:50,977
It was because you were biting your lips.

450
00:37:51,602 --> 00:37:52,979
And yesterday…

451
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:54,730
Well…

452
00:37:55,231 --> 00:37:57,275
And yesterday, that secretary thing!

453
00:37:57,358 --> 00:37:58,192
Sorry?

454
00:37:58,276 --> 00:38:01,404
You told Choi Do-yoon
you were my secretary.

455
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:06,617
That freaking jerk of a cousin of yours?

456
00:38:06,701 --> 00:38:07,910
What about it?

457
00:38:08,494 --> 00:38:11,831
We have a contract,
and this has to stay secret,

458
00:38:11,914 --> 00:38:13,457
so I had to think fast.

459
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:16,294
Then use that quick thinking of yours
to fix this mess!

460
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:18,796
I…

461
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:22,675
I came in here to say that.

462
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:25,636
Are you telling me to pretend
to be your secretary?

463
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:29,932
I need to write a script.
I don't even know what secretaries do.

464
00:38:30,016 --> 00:38:32,852
Just sit at your desk.
You'll still get paid, of course.

465
00:38:32,935 --> 00:38:34,729
Forget the salary.

466
00:38:34,812 --> 00:38:37,106
I have a script to finish in three months.

467
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:38,941
My future depends on it.

468
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:40,943
Then write it during work hours.

469
00:38:42,236 --> 00:38:44,864
So I get paid,
and I get to work on my script?

470
00:38:44,947 --> 00:38:47,700
If Choi Do-yoon finds out
you lied about being my secretary,

471
00:38:47,783 --> 00:38:50,703
he'll do anything to dig up my weaknesses.

472
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:53,164
You have no idea.

473
00:38:58,544 --> 00:38:59,462
Fine. I'll do it.

474
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:02,465
Really?

475
00:39:02,548 --> 00:39:06,177
I'm the one who lied
about being your secretary, after all.

476
00:39:09,764 --> 00:39:11,098
I'll be your secretary.

477
00:39:13,726 --> 00:39:14,560
All right.

478
00:39:15,644 --> 00:39:16,520
Then

479
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:19,565
let's go to work together tomorrow.

480
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:23,527
Okay, then.

481
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:25,154
Morning charge now.

482
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:39,377
That's just the sound it makes
while charging.

483
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:42,380
Yeah, sure.
I have to go to the TV station today.

484
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:46,175
I'll probably be back in the evening.
It should last until then, right?

485
00:39:55,267 --> 00:39:56,852
Don't you have work to do?

486
00:39:56,936 --> 00:39:59,563
Are you going to keep following me?
I'm here to work.

487
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:00,564
Go do your thing.

488
00:40:00,648 --> 00:40:04,026
I'm just trying to stay close
in case anything happens.

489
00:40:04,527 --> 00:40:06,362
I'll be at the café downstairs.

490
00:40:06,862 --> 00:40:09,573
Huh? You know there's a café here?

491
00:40:10,157 --> 00:40:11,409
Have you been here before?

492
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:17,164
This is where we first met, remember?

493
00:40:18,082 --> 00:40:20,334
Oh. You're right.

494
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,962
And this is where we had our first kiss.

495
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:26,632
Well…

496
00:40:27,133 --> 00:40:29,510
I'll go get some work done.

497
00:40:29,593 --> 00:40:32,847
Go grab a coffee at the café downstairs
or something.

498
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:55,119
What do you think?

499
00:41:01,417 --> 00:41:02,251
Ms. Na.

500
00:41:03,752 --> 00:41:04,587
Yes?

501
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:08,716
See? I knew you could do it.

502
00:41:09,383 --> 00:41:10,217
Is it okay?

503
00:41:10,301 --> 00:41:11,135
Bo-bae.

504
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:13,637
This scene is super romantic.
What's gotten into you?

505
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:15,806
This is what I was talking about.

506
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:17,683
A beer kiss? I love it!

507
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:19,477
It's natural. It feels real.

508
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:21,645
I had to stop and savor every word.

509
00:41:21,729 --> 00:41:24,607
My mouth is still watering, see?
I can't make it stop.

510
00:41:25,191 --> 00:41:26,400
Pretty good, huh?

511
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:29,153
Even as I was writing it,
I knew I'd nailed it.

512
00:41:29,236 --> 00:41:30,779
Seriously, how did you do it?

513
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:32,573
Are you seeing someone or what?

514
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:35,910
-No.
-She's not?

515
00:41:35,993 --> 00:41:36,994
Huh? No.

516
00:41:37,745 --> 00:41:38,829
Well, whatever.

517
00:41:38,913 --> 00:41:40,831
And this one. The Hangang River scene.

518
00:41:40,915 --> 00:41:43,584
It's a bit cliché, but I love it.

519
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:46,795
"He got hurt for me,
but he only cares if I'm okay."

520
00:41:46,879 --> 00:41:48,130
That's what I'm like!

521
00:41:49,965 --> 00:41:54,345
Bo-bae has been an expert
on romance novels, movies, and comics

522
00:41:54,428 --> 00:41:56,096
since she was little.

523
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:58,307
I guess it's finally paying off!

524
00:41:58,390 --> 00:42:02,019
Yeah, I think so too. She's got it.
She's got the hang of it!

525
00:42:02,102 --> 00:42:05,523
You're right.
I think I've got the hang of it.

526
00:42:05,606 --> 00:42:07,191
Keep this up, okay?

527
00:42:07,274 --> 00:42:10,569
Next episode, then the next,
all the way to the finale. Okay?

528
00:42:10,653 --> 00:42:12,279
How about a dance, everyone?

529
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:14,114
She's got the hang of it

530
00:42:14,198 --> 00:42:15,491
Got the hang of it, hey!

531
00:42:15,574 --> 00:42:17,368
Na Bo-bae's got the hang of it

532
00:42:17,451 --> 00:42:18,452
Hey!

533
00:42:19,161 --> 00:42:20,746
Today's meeting is important, okay?

534
00:42:20,829 --> 00:42:23,207
If this goes well,
you'll make your Hollywood debut.

535
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:25,334
I'm so nervous.

536
00:42:25,834 --> 00:42:27,670
Hey, no need to be nervous.

537
00:42:27,753 --> 00:42:29,505
You speak great English.

538
00:42:29,588 --> 00:42:31,423
You're ready for this, dude.

539
00:42:34,260 --> 00:42:35,094
One sec.

540
00:42:36,887 --> 00:42:38,305
Hello, Director.

541
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:40,182
We're almost there.

542
00:42:41,517 --> 00:42:43,602
You mean right now?

543
00:42:45,479 --> 00:42:46,689
It's Bo-bae.

544
00:42:47,356 --> 00:42:48,190
Yes.

545
00:42:49,650 --> 00:42:52,194
Of course. Eun-ho's always ready.

546
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:55,239
Every time I look away, that punk…

547
00:42:55,322 --> 00:42:58,117
Sorry? Oh, no,
I wasn't talking to you, sir.

548
00:42:58,200 --> 00:42:59,577
Of course not.

549
00:43:01,245 --> 00:43:02,788
Sorry I kept you waiting.

550
00:43:02,871 --> 00:43:05,708
I got a lot of compliments today.

551
00:43:06,208 --> 00:43:09,044
Are you a kid?
Getting excited over compliments?

552
00:43:15,134 --> 00:43:16,135
Bo-bae.

553
00:43:17,511 --> 00:43:19,430
Eun-ho. What are you doing here?

554
00:43:19,513 --> 00:43:20,806
Hello, Mr. Ji Eun-ho.

555
00:43:21,390 --> 00:43:22,349
Hello.

556
00:43:24,852 --> 00:43:27,605
I'm just here for a meeting.
What are you doing here?

557
00:43:27,688 --> 00:43:30,941
I met with Director Yeom and Seo-jeong
for feedback on the script.

558
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:33,527
And this is?

559
00:43:34,486 --> 00:43:35,821
Oh, he's…

560
00:43:36,864 --> 00:43:38,657
just a friend.

561
00:43:39,867 --> 00:43:43,412
I didn't know you had a friend like him.

562
00:43:44,413 --> 00:43:47,708
He's a friend and a source.
We met through work recently.

563
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:50,836
Good to see you again. I'm Baek Ho-rang.

564
00:43:52,046 --> 00:43:54,757
Through work, Ms. Na Bo-bae and I

565
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:57,384
have been getting pretty close recently.

566
00:43:58,844 --> 00:44:00,804
I'm sure you already know my name.

567
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:03,140
I met Ms. Na when she made her debut,

568
00:44:03,223 --> 00:44:06,018
and we've been very close ever since.

569
00:44:15,027 --> 00:44:16,904
Did you two know each other?

570
00:44:17,780 --> 00:44:19,323
He's high up at TS Resort.

571
00:44:19,406 --> 00:44:21,617
Yeah, that's right.

572
00:44:23,619 --> 00:44:26,330
I got a secretary job at TS Resort
for my research.

573
00:44:26,413 --> 00:44:28,040
For about three months.

574
00:44:28,123 --> 00:44:31,168
So I can't really call him my friend.
He's my boss, really.

575
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:34,463
Oh, your boss?

576
00:44:34,546 --> 00:44:36,757
Then you two are probably not that close.

577
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:38,092
Not that close?

578
00:44:38,175 --> 00:44:40,177
Ms. Na and I

579
00:44:40,260 --> 00:44:42,388
have been stuck together like glue lately.

580
00:44:43,347 --> 00:44:46,517
That's what a secretary does, you know.

581
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:50,270
It's great you're so dedicated,

582
00:44:50,354 --> 00:44:51,897
but take care of yourself too.

583
00:44:56,777 --> 00:44:59,571
You know I was the male lead
in her debut show, right?

584
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:03,158
Oh, that show. Wistful something, right?

585
00:45:03,242 --> 00:45:05,369
Yes, Wistful Youth.

586
00:45:05,452 --> 00:45:06,286
Did you watch it?

587
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:08,205
No, not yet.

588
00:45:09,289 --> 00:45:11,583
You should watch it.
It's a real masterpiece.

589
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:17,798
I fell for her back then,
and I've been following her ever since.

590
00:45:17,881 --> 00:45:20,050
Ms. Na here is a really good writer.

591
00:45:20,134 --> 00:45:21,969
Stop it, Eun-ho.

592
00:45:22,594 --> 00:45:23,971
What? It's true.

593
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:26,807
If you ask me to be the lead,
I'll come running.

594
00:45:26,890 --> 00:45:29,309
If you want to be the lead, I'd totally--

595
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:32,646
A big star like you must be busy.
We shouldn't keep you.

596
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:36,024
I'll be in touch soon.

597
00:45:41,947 --> 00:45:43,449
What? Why is he leaving alone?

598
00:45:44,199 --> 00:45:47,369
Well, I'll call you later, Eun-ho.

599
00:45:47,453 --> 00:45:48,287
Bye.

600
00:45:48,787 --> 00:45:50,581
Hey, why are you leaving alone?

601
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,223
Well done. You all worked so hard.

602
00:46:08,307 --> 00:46:09,975
-I'm good.
-Well done. Great work!

603
00:46:10,058 --> 00:46:12,811
Our show's called Wistful Youth,

604
00:46:13,312 --> 00:46:15,481
but our ratings
will be anything but wistful!

605
00:46:15,564 --> 00:46:16,732
Anything but wistful!

606
00:46:17,483 --> 00:46:20,319
-Anything but wistful!
-Anything but wistful!

607
00:46:20,402 --> 00:46:21,236
Wistful!

608
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:23,489
Youth!

609
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:25,324
Great work, team!

610
00:46:25,407 --> 00:46:26,575
Great work!

611
00:46:26,658 --> 00:46:28,869
Huh? Where's Ms. Na?

612
00:46:28,952 --> 00:46:31,288
-She's outside. I'll get her.
-She should be here.

613
00:46:31,371 --> 00:46:32,331
Yes.

614
00:46:32,414 --> 00:46:33,582
Have a seat, sir!

615
00:46:33,665 --> 00:46:34,917
-Seo-jeong!
-Yes, sir!

616
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:36,293
You did great.

617
00:46:36,376 --> 00:46:37,920
-Me? Really?
-Yeah.

618
00:46:38,003 --> 00:46:38,879
Ms. Na.

619
00:46:39,588 --> 00:46:40,798
Ms. Na, are you okay?

620
00:46:43,050 --> 00:46:45,552
The director is looking for you.
Are you drunk?

621
00:46:57,898 --> 00:46:58,732
Ms. Na.

622
00:47:01,443 --> 00:47:05,656
If you think you're too drunk
to remember this,

623
00:47:06,448 --> 00:47:07,950
can I tell you something?

624
00:47:11,411 --> 00:47:12,830
To tell you the truth,

625
00:47:13,622 --> 00:47:14,623
I've

626
00:47:15,123 --> 00:47:16,667
liked you since…

627
00:47:21,755 --> 00:47:22,840
That stings!

628
00:47:24,550 --> 00:47:25,384
Nope!

629
00:47:26,802 --> 00:47:29,137
What was that just now?

630
00:47:29,721 --> 00:47:31,223
Do you think it'll work out?

631
00:47:31,306 --> 00:47:35,227
Even the slightest touch from me zaps you.

632
00:47:35,727 --> 00:47:40,315
How can I date anyone?

633
00:47:53,871 --> 00:47:56,248
But what if someone still likes you?

634
00:47:59,084 --> 00:48:00,961
Is now really the time to date?

635
00:48:02,004 --> 00:48:04,673
Everyone's obsessed with dating.

636
00:48:04,756 --> 00:48:07,217
We should work!

637
00:48:07,301 --> 00:48:10,012
We should be successful first, you know?

638
00:48:10,512 --> 00:48:12,097
Once we're successful…

639
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:15,642
can we date then?

640
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:16,894
Of course.

641
00:48:16,977 --> 00:48:18,145
Really?

642
00:48:24,610 --> 00:48:26,361
They're probably not dating.

643
00:48:26,862 --> 00:48:28,739
She still has that power.

644
00:48:29,531 --> 00:48:32,200
So how is he okay?

645
00:48:33,118 --> 00:48:34,244
-What's going on?
-Sorry.

646
00:48:34,328 --> 00:48:35,370
Hey, Ji Eun-ho!

647
00:48:36,288 --> 00:48:38,790
Why are you here?
We're supposed to meet the director.

648
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:40,000
Right.

649
00:48:40,083 --> 00:48:42,085
Please put your phones away. No photos.

650
00:48:42,169 --> 00:48:43,128
I'm sorry.

651
00:48:43,211 --> 00:48:45,255
Let's go. Get a hold of yourself.

652
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:47,049
I'm sorry.

653
00:48:49,843 --> 00:48:53,639
Do you remember
the last term you added to the contract?

654
00:48:56,850 --> 00:48:59,144
"Neither of us shall see
anyone of the opposite gender"?

655
00:49:01,605 --> 00:49:02,814
You mean Eun-ho?

656
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:07,277
Eun-ho is just a close friend.

657
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:08,612
And my savior.

658
00:49:09,196 --> 00:49:10,197
Savior?

659
00:49:10,864 --> 00:49:14,284
Eun-ho was the only one
who stopped me from quitting the drama.

660
00:49:14,368 --> 00:49:16,536
He said he loved my writing

661
00:49:17,162 --> 00:49:20,624
and would act in it himself
to show everyone how amazing it was.

662
00:49:22,042 --> 00:49:23,627
He's such a cool fan, isn't he?

663
00:49:24,127 --> 00:49:26,213
Cool fan, my ass.

664
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:30,968
Did Mr. Baek hire a new secretary?

665
00:49:37,724 --> 00:49:39,851
I've never seen her before.

666
00:50:06,086 --> 00:50:08,296
-Good morning.
-Good morning, sir.

667
00:50:12,217 --> 00:50:15,595
This is my new personal secretary
starting today.

668
00:50:15,679 --> 00:50:18,557
She'll be working directly for me.

669
00:50:18,640 --> 00:50:20,142
Don't give her any other work.

670
00:50:21,560 --> 00:50:22,686
Ms. Na.

671
00:50:24,396 --> 00:50:26,690
Hello. I'm Na Bo-bae.

672
00:50:26,773 --> 00:50:30,569
I'll be assisting Mr. Baek Ho-rang…
I mean, the senior managing director.

673
00:50:30,652 --> 00:50:32,029
Nice to work with you all.

674
00:50:37,284 --> 00:50:41,413
I'm sure you've seen the articles
about my engagement to Director Han.

675
00:50:41,496 --> 00:50:43,540
For now, don't respond to them.

676
00:50:43,623 --> 00:50:45,542
Just say it's confidential.

677
00:50:46,126 --> 00:50:49,004
So, are you really getting married, sir?

678
00:50:49,504 --> 00:50:52,883
When I say it's confidential,
I mean it, Mr. Lee.

679
00:50:55,385 --> 00:50:57,763
That's all the executive office
needs to know.

680
00:50:57,846 --> 00:50:59,222
Yes, sir. My apologies.

681
00:50:59,306 --> 00:51:00,891
Get Ms. Na a desk.

682
00:51:01,725 --> 00:51:02,559
Yes, sir.

683
00:51:02,642 --> 00:51:05,145
Let's make today count too.

684
00:51:06,146 --> 00:51:07,147
Let's do this.

685
00:51:24,372 --> 00:51:26,625
You're wearing gloves?

686
00:51:27,876 --> 00:51:29,127
Aren't they uncomfortable?

687
00:51:30,128 --> 00:51:32,380
Oh, these…

688
00:51:33,090 --> 00:51:36,676
I'm a bit germophobic.

689
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:38,887
I see.

690
00:51:38,970 --> 00:51:42,182
A germophobic secretary?

691
00:51:43,266 --> 00:51:45,060
That won't be easy.

692
00:51:45,143 --> 00:51:47,187
Yes, sir. Got it.

693
00:51:48,063 --> 00:51:49,106
Ms. Na.

694
00:51:51,108 --> 00:51:52,400
Mr. Baek is asking for you.

695
00:51:53,693 --> 00:51:54,569
Me?

696
00:52:00,408 --> 00:52:01,451
What is it?

697
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:05,497
What have you been doing?

698
00:52:06,748 --> 00:52:09,251
I was just about to write my script.

699
00:52:09,334 --> 00:52:10,752
You said I could write.

700
00:52:10,836 --> 00:52:12,587
You said you wouldn't make me work.

701
00:52:12,671 --> 00:52:17,008
But you should at least look like
you're working.

702
00:52:26,476 --> 00:52:28,228
Please make a copy of this.

703
00:52:34,776 --> 00:52:36,153
Why are you wearing gloves?

704
00:52:36,236 --> 00:52:37,821
Mind your own business.

705
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:43,577
Tell Ms. Na to bring me
this week's report.

706
00:52:44,077 --> 00:52:46,955
Hey, ask Ms. Na
if she knows how to make a PowerPoint.

707
00:52:47,455 --> 00:52:50,333
Hey, get me sparkling water
from the break room.

708
00:52:50,417 --> 00:52:52,878
No, Ms. Na. Not you, Mr. Yoon.

709
00:53:09,895 --> 00:53:11,021
Sir.

710
00:53:14,065 --> 00:53:15,066
Yeah. Hey.

711
00:53:15,567 --> 00:53:16,401
Yeah.

712
00:53:17,235 --> 00:53:18,528
Is there something you need?

713
00:53:18,612 --> 00:53:20,030
Oh, just do your work.

714
00:53:20,113 --> 00:53:21,990
Sit down and get back to it.

715
00:53:25,493 --> 00:53:26,328
Ms. Na.

716
00:53:27,162 --> 00:53:30,707
We'll have to revise the schedule
we put together earlier today.

717
00:53:33,919 --> 00:53:34,753
Pardon?

718
00:53:34,836 --> 00:53:36,213
The schedule.

719
00:53:36,296 --> 00:53:38,590
That we put together earlier today.

720
00:53:39,257 --> 00:53:41,092
Right.

721
00:53:41,718 --> 00:53:44,429
Yes. Go on, sir.

722
00:53:45,096 --> 00:53:46,848
What does your new schedule
look like, sir?

723
00:53:47,474 --> 00:53:49,935
I'll be inspecting
the resort shoot site at 1 p.m.,

724
00:53:50,018 --> 00:53:52,395
and I'll attend a meeting
from 2 p.m. to 3 p.m.

725
00:53:52,479 --> 00:53:54,272
Then I'll receive a performance report

726
00:53:54,356 --> 00:53:56,775
from the lounge manager
between 3 p.m. and 3:30 p.m.

727
00:53:56,858 --> 00:54:00,237
From 3:30 p.m. to 6 p.m.,
I'll be reviewing and approving reports.

728
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:01,154
And at 6 p.m…

729
00:54:01,238 --> 00:54:03,448
Just quit your job and become a rapper.

730
00:54:03,531 --> 00:54:04,532
…leave work with me.

731
00:54:05,116 --> 00:54:07,160
You said I wouldn't have to work.
For fuck's sake.

732
00:54:07,244 --> 00:54:08,662
Did you get all that?

733
00:54:08,745 --> 00:54:11,331
Yes, I wrote it down exactly.

734
00:54:18,380 --> 00:54:22,133
So, how's the rebranding project going?

735
00:54:22,217 --> 00:54:24,511
Our team is developing the concept.

736
00:54:24,594 --> 00:54:27,597
We plan to submit the draft
by the end of this week.

737
00:54:28,598 --> 00:54:32,811
How's the target analysis
and market research coming along?

738
00:54:33,478 --> 00:54:35,522
HE'S HEADING TO THE RESORT SHOOT SITE

739
00:54:50,745 --> 00:54:52,330
A NEW FEMALE SECRETARY HAS JOINED

740
00:54:52,414 --> 00:54:54,332
HE'S COMING IN
AFTER A PERSONAL APPOINTMENT

741
00:54:54,416 --> 00:54:55,917
HE'LL EAT AT HOME WITH HIS FAMILY

742
00:55:09,097 --> 00:55:12,142
I think they're filming something here.

743
00:55:12,225 --> 00:55:14,853
This is our first time sponsoring
a drama shoot location.

744
00:55:14,936 --> 00:55:16,104
A drama?

745
00:55:16,187 --> 00:55:17,981
Never been to a mini-series set, right?

746
00:55:18,898 --> 00:55:20,108
Take a good look.

747
00:55:20,734 --> 00:55:22,277
That's why I brought you here.

748
00:55:34,748 --> 00:55:38,126
I'll go talk to the person in charge.
Wait here for a moment.

749
00:55:47,802 --> 00:55:49,512
Why is Director Yeom here?

750
00:55:50,013 --> 00:55:52,057
He thinks I'm busy working on the script.

751
00:55:54,559 --> 00:55:55,602
I'm sorry.

752
00:55:57,228 --> 00:55:58,104
Bo-bae.

753
00:55:58,813 --> 00:56:00,065
Ju-hee.

754
00:56:04,986 --> 00:56:05,987
What the…

755
00:56:06,946 --> 00:56:07,864
What?

756
00:56:08,990 --> 00:56:10,033
What the hell?

757
00:56:10,617 --> 00:56:11,826
When does filming start?

758
00:56:11,910 --> 00:56:12,911
Why are you here?

759
00:56:12,994 --> 00:56:16,664
This is my resort,
so of course I should be here.

760
00:56:17,999 --> 00:56:20,960
But everyone seems so relaxed.

761
00:56:21,044 --> 00:56:23,838
Oh man. Don't you worry.

762
00:56:23,922 --> 00:56:26,800
We won't slack off
or go over the schedule, sir.

763
00:56:26,883 --> 00:56:28,426
Go tell the actors to gather.

764
00:56:28,510 --> 00:56:30,261
Have them use the back gate.

765
00:56:30,345 --> 00:56:31,429
-Okay?
-Got it.

766
00:56:32,722 --> 00:56:33,681
Who's that?

767
00:56:35,350 --> 00:56:36,434
Isn't that Ms. Na?

768
00:56:38,144 --> 00:56:39,479
Yeah, it is.

769
00:56:40,105 --> 00:56:41,314
She came with me.

770
00:56:41,898 --> 00:56:43,316
How do you know her?

771
00:56:43,983 --> 00:56:45,777
Right, you asked me
about her the other day.

772
00:56:48,071 --> 00:56:49,322
What's with you two?

773
00:56:56,454 --> 00:56:58,706
Are you one of the guys
lining up to date her?

774
00:56:59,958 --> 00:57:00,834
"Lining up"?

775
00:57:00,917 --> 00:57:02,544
She told me the other day.

776
00:57:02,627 --> 00:57:05,922
She said she was popular
and had guys lining up to go out with her.

777
00:57:06,673 --> 00:57:08,007
I knew it.

778
00:57:08,091 --> 00:57:11,678
No wonder her script
has been getting better recently.

779
00:57:15,432 --> 00:57:18,768
If Ms. Kang finds out about this,
she's going to flip out.

780
00:57:19,477 --> 00:57:20,645
What are you doing here?

781
00:57:22,313 --> 00:57:23,648
Did Director Yeom call you?

782
00:57:25,608 --> 00:57:27,068
Well, I…

783
00:57:29,404 --> 00:57:30,488
I'm here for work.

784
00:57:32,198 --> 00:57:34,534
You work part-time at TS Resort?

785
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:36,202
Well…

786
00:57:37,203 --> 00:57:38,121
Yeah.

787
00:57:38,204 --> 00:57:41,040
Didn't you work at a café before?

788
00:57:41,624 --> 00:57:44,043
You really work hard, Bo-bae.

789
00:57:44,127 --> 00:57:47,088
I'm so busy writing
I don't have time to do anything else.

790
00:57:48,673 --> 00:57:50,341
Gosh, what's with that face?

791
00:57:50,842 --> 00:57:54,512
You're so intimidating.
I can't even show that I care.

792
00:57:57,140 --> 00:57:57,974
Who's that?

793
00:57:58,558 --> 00:57:59,434
No way!

794
00:58:00,101 --> 00:58:02,520
Is that Baek Ho-rang?

795
00:58:03,354 --> 00:58:04,189
What?

796
00:58:04,272 --> 00:58:06,149
The guy next to Director Yeom.

797
00:58:06,649 --> 00:58:08,818
The one who's looking at me now.

798
00:58:08,902 --> 00:58:11,613
Ho-rang? What, like a tiger?

799
00:58:12,322 --> 00:58:13,990
That's a person's name?

800
00:58:17,827 --> 00:58:19,913
You don't even know the TS heir?

801
00:58:20,830 --> 00:58:23,750
You need to know their world too.

802
00:58:23,833 --> 00:58:25,251
You're a writer, after all.

803
00:58:25,335 --> 00:58:27,712
What Korean drama doesn't have
a chaebol character?

804
00:58:28,713 --> 00:58:30,548
Oh, yeah. Right.

805
00:58:31,799 --> 00:58:33,092
Actually,

806
00:58:33,718 --> 00:58:35,011
there was a rumor

807
00:58:35,094 --> 00:58:37,722
that he stays out of the media
because he's ugly.

808
00:58:38,640 --> 00:58:40,475
He could pass for an actor.

809
00:58:41,893 --> 00:58:44,312
There's something weird
about their relationship.

810
00:58:44,395 --> 00:58:49,859
To be precise, Ms. Kang sees Ms. Na
as a threat and doesn't like her.

811
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:52,487
I thought they were close.

812
00:58:52,570 --> 00:58:53,821
Close, my ass.

813
00:58:53,905 --> 00:58:57,367
Ms. Kang is jealous of Ms. Na.

814
00:58:57,450 --> 00:58:59,410
She's doing much better than Ms. Na,

815
00:58:59,494 --> 00:59:02,622
but she always looks down on her
in front of other people.

816
00:59:03,164 --> 00:59:04,832
I don't get why she's like that.

817
00:59:05,333 --> 00:59:07,669
He must be here to see me.

818
00:59:08,169 --> 00:59:09,671
I heard he's a fan of mine.

819
00:59:10,713 --> 00:59:11,548
Fan?

820
00:59:11,631 --> 00:59:14,801
I've written several shows, you know.

821
00:59:17,220 --> 00:59:20,265
Still, nothing beats
having Ji Eun-ho as your fan

822
00:59:20,348 --> 00:59:22,433
and following you around.

823
00:59:22,517 --> 00:59:24,227
I need to work harder.

824
00:59:30,275 --> 00:59:31,484
Here he comes.

825
00:59:40,410 --> 00:59:42,996
I'm Baek Ho-rang,
senior managing director at TS Resort.

826
00:59:43,663 --> 00:59:46,749
I'm Kang Ju-hee, the writer of this drama.

827
00:59:47,500 --> 00:59:48,585
Ms. Na.

828
00:59:49,919 --> 00:59:51,254
Do you like the resort?

829
00:59:53,464 --> 00:59:57,093
We at TS are interested
in sponsoring your next show,

830
00:59:57,176 --> 00:59:59,345
so we've sent you several proposals.

831
01:00:00,305 --> 01:00:02,515
But you haven't given us an answer.

832
01:00:03,349 --> 01:00:06,519
That's why you came here
with me today, right?

833
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:08,062
To inspect the site.

834
01:00:10,023 --> 01:00:10,857
Pardon?

835
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:13,401
Do you know Bo-bae?

836
01:00:13,484 --> 01:00:14,819
Of course I do.

837
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:16,154
I am

838
01:00:17,155 --> 01:00:18,740
a huge fan

839
01:00:19,991 --> 01:00:21,701
of Ms. Na Bo-bae, you see.

840
01:02:08,891 --> 01:02:13,521
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
